{"absent":["Completion wait and wake semantics beyond init and reinit.","Simple wait queue layout and blocking behavior.","Cpuset branch key lifecycle and enabled-state transitions.","Delay accounting timestamp arithmetic and reporting path.","Energy model registration, update and teardown lifecycle."],"dossier":"D01","findings":[{"kind":"struct","sids":["include/linux/completion.h::completion","include/linux/completion.h::init_completion","include/linux/completion.h::reinit_completion"],"text":"Completion object pairs a signal count with a simple wait queue; setup clears the count and prepares the queue while reset only clears the count."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["include/linux/completion.h::DECLARE_COMPLETION","include/linux/completion.h::DECLARE_COMPLETION_ONSTACK.alt_1","include/linux/completion.h::DECLARE_COMPLETION_ONSTACK.alt_2"],"text":"Static and on-stack declaration helpers yield zero-initialized completions, with alternate builds mapping on-stack form to dynamic setup or plain static setup."},{"kind":"export","sids":["include/linux/completion.h::init_completion","include/linux/completion.h::reinit_completion"],"text":"Init and reinit are small inline interfaces that establish or restore the unsignaled condition for a completion."},{"kind":"lock","sids":["include/linux/sched/task.h::task_lock"],"text":"Task allocation lock is taken and released around short critical sections through paired helpers."},{"kind":"lock","sids":["include/linux/cpuset.h::read_mems_allowed_begin.alt_1","include/linux/cpuset.h::read_mems_allowed_retry.alt_1"],"text":"Mems allowance updates serialize under task lock with interrupts masked and a sequence counter bracketing the store; readers sample then retry through that counter."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["include/linux/cpuset.h::cpusets_enabled.alt_1","include/linux/cpuset.h::cpusets_enabled.alt_2","include/linux/cpuset.h::__cpuset_zone_allowed.alt_1","include/linux/cpuset.h::__cpuset_zone_allowed.alt_2","include/linux/cpuset.h::cpuset_zone_allowed.alt_2"],"text":"Cpuset queries have enabled and disabled builds: enabled build consults branch state and node allowance, disabled build returns fixed permissive values."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["include/linux/delayacct.h::task_delay_info"],"text":"Delay record holds a raw spinlock plus per-class start stamps, accumulated delays, min and max bounds, counts, and max timestamps across block, swap, reclaim, thrash, compact, copy and irq classes."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["include/linux/delayacct.h::delayacct_tsk_init.alt_1","include/linux/delayacct.h::delayacct_tsk_free.alt_1","include/linux/delayacct.h::delayacct_init"],"text":"Delay helpers act only when a global switch is active and the task record exists; lifecycle init clears an inherited pointer then conditionally allocates, while free releases and nulls."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["include/linux/energy_model.h::em_perf_state"],"text":"Performance state entry carries capacity, frequency, power, derived cost and flags attributes."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["include/linux/energy_model.h::em_perf_table"],"text":"Performance table couples deferred reclamation and reference counting headers with trailing variable-length state storage."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["include/linux/energy_model.h::em_perf_domain"],"text":"Performance domain holds a protected table pointer, list linkage, identity, state count and bounds, flags, plus trailing CPU set storage."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/linux/energy_model.h::EM_PERF_STATE_INEFFICIENT"],"text":"One state flag marks an inefficient performance state."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/linux/energy_model.h::EM_PERF_DOMAIN_MICROWATTS"],"text":"Domain flags distinguish microwatt units, skipping inefficient states, and artificial domains, with helpers exposing CPU span and artificial test."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/linux/energy_model.h::EM_MAX_POWER"],"text":"Abstract power scale has an upper bound corresponding to sixty four watts."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/linux/energy_model.h::EM_MAX_NUM_CPUS.alt_1","include/linux/energy_model.h::EM_MAX_NUM_CPUS.alt_2"],"text":"Builds define distinct upper limits on CPUs covered by the energy model."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["include/linux/energy_model.h::em_data_callback.alt_1","include/linux/energy_model.h::em_data_callback.alt_2"],"text":"Registration callback bundle optionally supplies power lookup by frequency and cost lookup; disabled builds reduce it to an empty placeholder with neutral constructors."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["include/linux/energy_model.h::em_pd_get_efficient_state"],"text":"Efficient-state search returns the first state within configured bounds meeting requested utilization, optionally skipping inefficient entries, else the top bound."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["include/linux/energy_model.h::em_cpu_energy.alt_1"],"text":"CPU energy estimate returns zero for idle domains, otherwise clamps demand, selects a state, and scales that state cost by total utilization under read-side protection."},{"kind":"export","sids":["include/linux/energy_model.h::em_pd_nr_perf_states.alt_1","include/linux/energy_model.h::em_perf_state_from_pd.alt_1"],"text":"Helpers expose state count and dereferenced state array from a domain."},{"kind":"hazard","sids":["include/linux/completion.h::reinit_completion"],"text":"Reset clears the completion count without touching the wait queue, so concurrent waiter handling must be addressed outside these fragments."},{"kind":"hazard","sids":["include/linux/energy_model.h::em_cpu_energy.alt_1","include/linux/energy_model.h::em_perf_state_from_pd.alt_1"],"text":"Energy read path asserts read-side coverage and dereferences the table through that mechanism, so callers must hold the read side."},{"kind":"entry_point","sids":["include/linux/cpuset.h::cpusets_insane_config.alt_2","include/linux/delayacct.h::delayacct_init"],"text":"Cpuset and delay accounting initializers appear as t